cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it."
title: "Ternary Security Agent: evaluation methodology for sub-2-bit compressed tool-calling agents"
abstract: >-
  An open research programme asking whether sub-2-bit (1.58-bit) weight
  compression can preserve cybersecurity, code, and tool-calling capability
  well enough to run as an autonomous security agent. The repository's current
  contribution is methodological: aggregate scores measurably under-report
  compression damage in tool-calling agents, and per-channel error rates plus
  success under tightened error budgets expose what the aggregate hides.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Zaidux/ternary-secagent"
keywords:
  - quantization
  - ternary-compression
  - low-bit-llm
  - agent-evaluation
  - cybersecurity
  - tool-calling
authors:
